What it's about
Responsibilities

Your main duties and responsibilities comprise the following tasks:

- Source investment opportunities in thematic areas of focus for Partners Group Infrastructure

- Discuss relevant factors about each investment opportunity that he/she is working on, with the firm’s senior managers

- Quantitative and qualitative analysis on prospective direct equity investments in companies in the infrastructure sector in Asia-Pacific

- Own and run complex financial models across various infrastructure sub-sectors

- Conduct strategic & financial analysis of various sectors and companies of interest

- Develop relevant investment themes and target companies within that thematic across Asia Pacific

- Prepare Investment Committee papers for Investment Committee in Partners Group’s template. Attend and participate in Investment Committee meetings on a regular basis

- Lead transaction due diligence work-streams, including financial, commercial, legal, tax, etc.

- Actively participate in meetings with current and prospective target companies. Undertake on-site visits, etc.

- Support investment leadership in securing debt arrangements, negotiating purchase/sale agreements, shareholders’ agreements, employment agreements and incentive compensation for management teams of portfolio companies

- Work closely with portfolio companies and portfolio management teams in Asia Pacific to implement Partners Group’s underwritten value creation plan

- Conduct various tasks related to product reporting, monitoring investments, market research, and marketing efforts

