Specific responsibilities will include leading investment diligence and underwriting in all respects, including the following specific tasks:

- Apply critical thinking and judgment in prioritizing investment opportunities;

- Prepare industry and competitive research on industrials and specific businessesd;

- Lead construction of detailed, business unit-based financial models, including optimal capital structure, purchase price, adjustments and sensitivities to economic conditions;

- Draft investment committee reports while supervising external resources in the process;

- Interact with third party due diligence partners (tax professionals, attorneys, technical consultants, insurance, environmental, etc.);

- Assist in negotiating debt facilities and support the Deal Captain in negotiating purchase agreements, employment agreements and incentive compensation for management teams;

- Flex both upwards and downwards in order to coordinate the investment process and ensure every aspect of tdhe work gets done.

- Act proactively in all matters arising in the ordinary course of investment management, acting quickly to identify, address and correct issues;

- Identify and evaluate strategic opportunities such as acquisitions, divestitures, or entering new market/verticals;

- Provide support in investment exit process management.

What it's about

The Private Equity Internship is an opportunity for a young professional with top credentials to launch into a career with a world-leading Private Equity buy-out manager and join their investment team. As part of this internship, you will support the Private Equity Services buy-out team on all aspects related to sourcing and execution of private equity investments and portfolio management.

We are looking for a candidate to join the team in January 2027 for 6 months.

Responsibilities:

- Assessing and valuing prospective investment opportunities

- Modeling business plans, LBO structures and investment returns

- Participating actively in due diligence workstreams on prospective investments (e.g. financial, commercial, ESG, tax and legal due diligence)

- Drafting internal investment recommendation documents

- Conducting various other tasks related to sourcing, market research, product reporting and marketing

