What it's about

We are looking for a Credit Research Senior Associate to join our US Liquid Credit investment team in New York, where we manage leveraged loans and high yield bonds for multiple CLOs, open-end, and closed-end funds. Our global team of 25 investment professionals has issued 40 CLOs+ to date and manages over USD 20bn of AUM.

This individual will:

- Serve as primary analyst for one or more sectors, owning end-to-end credit coverage

- Back-up other analysts on the team and assist portfolio managers with projects and assignments, as needed

- Conduct in-depth fundamental credit analysis on corporate issuers, including financial statement analysis, cash flow modeling, and capital structure review

- Prepare credit investment memos and present investment recommendations to the Investment Committee and portfolio managers

- Proactively monitor existing investments "real time", providing timely updates on company performance and related matters

- Develop in-depth knowledge of assigned sectors and follow relevant industry developments

- Provide regular input on structural, secular, and cyclical themes affecting credits and industries covered

- Interact with corporate issuers, arranger banks, and other market stakeholders to develop and enhance familiarity with assigned issuers and sectors

- Participate in daily/weekly team meetings to discuss current business activity, financial performance, and events related to credits covered

- Review credit agreements and other legal documentation related to issuers

